WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:08.220
Graft a second notochord against the side of a chick neural tube.

2
00:00:08.860 --> 00:00:12.420
The neural cells beside it start to behave like floor plate.

3
00:00:13.060 --> 00:00:15.200
The tube gains a second bottom.

4
00:00:16.040 --> 00:00:20.220
So how does a cell in the wall know how far it sits from the bottom?

5
00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:23.700
The answer is a signal called Sonic hedgehog.

6
00:00:25.183 --> 00:00:29.423
The floor plate and the notochord both make Sonic hedgehog.

7
00:00:30.203 --> 00:00:33.363
It spreads up the wall and falls off with distance.

8
00:00:34.563 --> 00:00:38.723
A signal that spreads from a source and gives different instructions at different

9
00:00:38.723 --> 00:00:41.323
concentrations is called a morphogen.

10
00:00:42.483 --> 00:00:44.443
Cells low in the wall receive a lot.

11
00:00:45.223 --> 00:00:46.983
Cells high in the wall receive little.

12
00:00:47.867 --> 00:00:51.007
Each cell answers with transcription factors.

13
00:00:51.987 --> 00:00:56.827
Class I factors are repressed by Sonic hedgehog, so they are lost where the signal

14
00:00:56.827 --> 00:01:02.427
is high. Class II factors need the signal, so they appear where it is high.

15
00:01:03.647 --> 00:01:07.847
Pax7 is switched off by low levels, so it marks the dorsal half.

16
00:01:08.867 --> 00:01:13.567
Nkx2.2 needs high levels, and it sits next to the floor plate.

17
00:01:14.350 --> 00:01:16.770
But cells read more than the level.

18
00:01:17.770 --> 00:01:23.030
Sonic hedgehog switches on its own receptor, Patched1, so cells grow less

19
00:01:23.030 --> 00:01:24.910
sensitive and signaling fades.

20
00:01:25.790 --> 00:01:28.370
A higher dose keeps signaling going longer.

21
00:01:29.170 --> 00:01:33.910
At a fixed dose, longer exposure gives progressively more ventral identities.

22
00:01:34.870 --> 00:01:40.430
In this model, a cell's identity tracks something like the total signaling it has
received.

23
00:01:40.700 --> 00:01:45.800
A smooth slope should give a blur, yet the borders are sharp.

24
00:01:46.900 --> 00:01:50.120
Factors on either side of a border repress each other.

25
00:01:51.100 --> 00:01:58.060
Pax6 and Nkx2.2 do this where the motor neuron domain meets the domain below.

26
00:01:59.080 --> 00:02:03.140
Two such factors form a switch with two stable states.

27
00:02:03.900 --> 00:02:07.880
A cell near the border falls to one side, and stays there.

28
00:02:08.650 --> 00:02:12.310
The result is five ventral stripes of progenitors.

29
00:02:12.950 --> 00:02:20.290
From top to bottom they are p0, p1, p2, pMN and p3.

30
00:02:21.270 --> 00:02:28.630
They make V0, V1 and V2 interneurons, motor neurons, and V3 neurons.

31
00:02:29.690 --> 00:02:36.270
Keep this rule. A source makes a slope, cells read its level and its duration, and

32
00:02:36.270 --> 00:02:38.790
cross-repression sharpens it into domains.
